{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Every lamb speckled and patched.</b> That is, brown-speckled and patched specifically. But not sheep and he-goats and goats, and not ring-striped ones — and he even removed the ring-striped ones and the older males that he had set to breed from them, as it is written: ״ויסר ביום ההוא את התישים העקודים״. And this is great trickery, for the condition was not so; therefore Jacob made the rods split." "<b>Brown among the sheep.</b> But not among the goats, for most of them are brown. <b>Brown.</b> ro'sh in Old French."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:49.653304046Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}